845 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 175 0 R
/E (    Soil erosion, a major environmental hazard today is caused by both natural and man-made factors. Soil erosion is caused by unobstructed overflow and the flow of running water which carry away the topmost layer of the soil. Forest fires destroy the roots of plants which bind soil together and lead to erosion. )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
846 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 175 0 R
/E (      The effects of soil erosion are flood, drought etc. As vital nutrients of soil get wasted away, the soil turns barren. Soil erosion can be prevented by construction of dams, bunds etc. Afforestation helps prevent soil erosion as trees hold the soil together with roots. Improved agricultural methods such as contour ploughing also check soil erosion.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
